{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1302998-kinain-heritages-which-would-you-take","id":1302998,"title":"Kinain Heritages - which would you take?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-05T20:50:23-07:00","id":1302998,"title":"Kinain Heritages - which would you take?","content":"So, by my math, if you're willing to be hella cheesy, a Kinain (using the original rules, not the C20 version) could mathematically take up to five instances of the Honored Birthright Fae Gift (if you have Fae Blood 5, you can take five separate gifts; you get five traits of gifts to start, can take five Fae Marks, and start with enough Freebies to buy three more, the cap under Fae Blood 5). This is obviously, as I said, real cheesy... but what the hell, sometimes it's fun to cut loose a bit!<br /> <br /> So, if you were a Kinain of such rarefied power, which five Heritages (and thus sets of birthrights) would you pick and why?<br /> <br /> I think I'd go with Eshu for sure - the storytelling benefits are really helpful for me as a story teller (and Storyteller), and either the Serendipity or Spirit Pathways birthrights would be really useful (they seem to more or less be the same thing with different details in any event... since we're playing by the earlier rules, though, I'll call it Spirit Pathways). The Clurichaun are also almost certainly on my list - the vanishing ability could come in handy (and just be fun for Batman-like shenanigans), and the Insight Ability would be really beneficial in a conversation.<br /> <br /> As for the other three... I'm a bit less certain. There's a lot of good choices, and that makes it hard to pick. Boggans' helpfulness and productivity would be handy too... if I could clean apartment in a fraction of the time, I'd do it. Nockers are cool too, though... forging chimera and making objects work by looking at them would be nifty, and you'd get to hang out with Etherites as well (and, if the ST in the sky is generous, maybe even pick up a few sorcerous tricks at the least). If it was a world where we knew that there were gifts and powers that could embarrass you, the Sidhe would be a certain pick, and the extra appearance isn't bad either. But, if I was just going for looks, the Merfolk or Selkie boons would be just as useful (actually, Merfolk would be especially broken... the ability to breathe under water and swim freely but NOT suffer the Coldness? They are a pretty good pick on that too). The pooka birthrights could also be helpful and fun - turning into an animal is usually cool (as long as you can go back), and dragging the truth out of people is really helpful when you can't read their emotions well naturally. I am also avoiding most of the Gallain since they belong to native cultures and are in no way part of my heritage (admittedly, a lot of the Kithain are specific to particular regions by name, but there is enough sharing and similarity that it's possible to make the arguments for them... plus, the Roman Empire mixed up those heritages pretty well by assigning soldiers to legions far from their homelands). And I'm iffy on claiming Dark-Kin and Thallain heritage... but you know what? Let's go with it. I don't think there's anything that says you can't choose those as a Heritage. And I know just which Dark-Kin I'd go with - the Moirae. Reading the fates around others can be helpful, and Fata could be useful when travelling.<br /> <br /> I think my picks would be:<br /> -Eshu<br /> -Clurichaun<br /> -Nocker<br /> -Merfolk<br /> -Moirae<br /> <br /> How about yours?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T21:53:07-07:00","id":1303474,"title":"","content":"Well, there are three that I can think of right off the top of my head, but the last two would be primarily speculation, so I don't think I'll be listing them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pooka</b> - Although shapeshifting is my most favorite power in all of mythology, there's another reason I'd pick these lovable tricksters. They are born from dreams of a life free of responsibility and worries. Something which I would sympathize quite strongly with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clurichaun</b> - I love the thrill of a good fight, and I love Celtic music. Taking Clurichaun seemed like an obvious choice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Autumn Sidhe</b> - If what my father says about my genealogy is correct, I'm descended from an Arch Duke of the French aristocracy. Which means I'm pretty much royalty, as far as I understand. Though it's clear my family's proud legacy has suffered heavily in the wake of the peasant uprising...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T19:18:18-07:00","id":1303692,"title":"","content":"Craftwork, Social Dynamics, Physical Prowess, Titan's Power, and either Spirit Pathways or FixIt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T20:35:11-07:00","id":1303703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1302998-kinain-heritages-which-would-you-take?p=1303692#post1303692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craftwork, Social Dynamics, Physical Prowess, Titan's Power, and either Spirit Pathways or FixIt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good choices... but I think you may be underselling yourself. The Gift actually lets you get BOTH Birthrights from the Heritage. IIRC, you've got five there with the Fixit (Boggans, Nockers, Satyrs, Trolls, and Eshu), so your'e probably good (and getting more than you bargained for in a good way).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}